  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:gy9_-Qbmzsk",
    "purpose": "Rank and review the 15 sweatshirt brands the creator's audience voted as the internet's favorites, from a $17 Amazon sweatshirt to a $391 Japanese one, comparing construction, fabric, fit, shrinkage and value.",
    "video_type": "ranking",
    "thesis": "Sweatshirts from the creator's audience poll, presented from least to most popular by votes, are judged on quality, feel, fit, shrinkage and overall value. A final value score for each appears in the description.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Brands are presented in order of audience votes, not quality. Champion was most voted (11.14%) and Buzz Rickson's second (6.19%). The creator's own overall-value scores and list are in the description.",
      "Loopwheel knitting is explained: low tension during knitting means the fabric is not stretched out and holds its shape better over time (Real McCoy's, Whitesville).",
      "Reverse weave is explained: Champion cut body fabric on the cross grain to stop lengthwise shrinkage, then added side rib panels to handle width shrinkage and add stretch.",
      "Uniqlo and Abercrombie & Fitch are contrasted: a basic, durable budget sweatshirt versus one heavily washed for softness with a high polyester content.",
      "Wonder Looper's 24 oz Fox Fibre crew is covered: a naturally colored cotton that must be blended with longer-staple cotton. It was received free and disqualified from the ranking.",
      "Shrinkage figures are given for most sweatshirts, e.g. Camber 12% width / 3% length, Real McCoy's 5% / 4.35%, Uniqlo 3.4% / 0%.",
      "Sizing notes: Reigning Champ should be sized down, Brut runs cropped (tall people size up), Camber has a very tight neck hole, American Giant suits bigger and taller guys.",
      "Buzz Rickson's versus Whitesville (both from the same parent company) is framed as mostly a choice about the 5x1 rib knit cuffs.",
      "Vintage Champion and vintage Russell were bought on eBay. Both turned out smaller than expected, likely women's or children's sizes."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Intro",
        "summary": "Teaser clips, then how the list was built: an audience poll tallied into percentages, with all 15 sweatshirts bought, worn, washed and assessed. Order runs from least to most popular.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "The Real McCoy's",
        "summary": "The 10 oz loopwheel sweatshirt, with an explanation of loopwheel versus tension knitting, the V-insert 'Dorito', the wide neckline, finish quality and shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Uniqlo",
        "summary": "Uniqlo's $40 sweatshirt, included to contrast with Abercrombie. Covers its sensible budget priorities, bound versus non-bound collars, and shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Camber",
        "summary": "A made-in-USA heavyweight sweatshirt with a coarse, 90s feel, a tight neck hole and cross-grain body. Covers its high shrinkage and 10% polyester in the heather color.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Arc Pulse sponsor",
        "summary": "Sponsor read for the Arc Pulse aluminum iPhone case, with a drop-test skit and discount code.",
        "first_segment": 4,
        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Abercrombie & Fitch",
        "summary": "The $60 Abercrombie sweatshirt that Taylor took over, prioritizing softness through heavy washing, with 30% polyester. Contrasted with Uniqlo's approach; shrinkage given.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 7
      },
      {
        "title": "Wonder Looper",
        "summary": "The limited-edition $391, 24 oz double-heavyweight Fox Fibre crew, received free from the founder. Explains Fox Fibre naturally colored cotton and its properties; pre-washed so no shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 7,
        "last_segment": 9
      },
      {
        "title": "Reigning Champ",
        "summary": "The heavyweight fleece crew: a likely one-off wavy ('bacon') collar, advice to size down, its dry hand feel, side gusset for mobility, and shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 9,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Vintage Champion and Vintage Russell",
        "summary": "eBay vintage purchases that turned out small. Covers the history and mechanics of Champion's reverse weave, Russell's origin story, a vintage Russell versus Champion comparison, and pilling.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 13
      },
      {
        "title": "Whitesville",
        "summary": "A Japanese loopwheel sweatshirt that is loose and fluffy-soft, with 5x1 rib knit cuffs, hem and collar and a minor stitching flaw. Pre-washed, zero shrink.",
        "first_segment": 13,
        "last_segment": 14
      },
      {
        "title": "American Giant",
        "summary": "An overbuilt heavyweight hoodie with reinforced arms, rib-knit shoulders and a big hood, recommended for bigger and taller guys; shrinkage given.",
        "first_segment": 14,
        "last_segment": 14
      },
      {
        "title": "Russell Athletic (current)",
        "summary": "The cheapest sweatshirt on the list, a 65/35 cotton-polyester 'cotton rich' blend: who it's for, likely pilling, and shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 14,
        "last_segment": 15
      },
      {
        "title": "Brut",
        "summary": "A small French brand that names its products 'the best'. Covers the very cropped, modern fit, sizing advice for tall people, ribbing feel and shrinkage.",
        "first_segment": 15,
        "last_segment": 16
      },
      {
        "title": "Buzz Rickson's",
        "summary": "Second most popular by votes: balanced weight and softness. Compared with Whitesville, which comes from the same parent company, mainly on cuff rib style; shrinkage given.",
        "first_segment": 16,
        "last_segment": 17
      },
      {
        "title": "Champion",
        "summary": "Most popular by votes. Covers the current reverse weave hoodie versus a 90s made-in-USA one, a price comparison with Abercrombie and Uniqlo, and the creator's sentimental first Champion.",
        "first_segment": 17,
        "last_segment": 18
      },
      {
        "title": "Outro",
        "summary": "Notes that the ranking reflects overall value to the creator, floats a possible part two, and teases a personal announcement.",
        "first_segment": 18,
        "last_segment": 19
      }
    ],
